{
  "_comment": [
    "LEGACY / SELF-HOSTED ONLY — NOT the authoritative memory config.",
    "This block wires the retired local-tunnel model: graphiti-memory reached at",
    "127.0.0.1:8100 via an SSH tunnel to the self-hosted Hetzner VPS, with the token",
    "pulled from GRAPHITI_MCP_TOKEN (macOS Keychain / ~/.cursor/secrets on that host).",
    "",
    "AUTHORITATIVE CONFIG: environment/claude-code/mcp.template.json — the hosted HTTP",
    "control plane (l9-shared-memory @ https://memory.quantumaipartners.com/mcp,",
    "Bearer ${L9_MEMORY_CLIENT_TOKEN}). Claude Code CLI/Web/Mobile use that; it supersedes",
    "this file and needs no SSH tunnel, no Keychain, and no VPS reachability.",
    "",
    "Keep this example ONLY if you are deliberately running the self-hosted VPS tunnel",
    "deployment. For every hosted/managed environment, ignore it and use the template above."
  ],
  "mcpServers": {
    "graphiti-memory": {
      "url": "http://127.0.0.1:8100/mcp/",
      "headers": {
        "Authorization": "Bearer ${GRAPHITI_MCP_TOKEN}"
      }
    }
  }
}
